  "subject": "A land surveyor knocks a boundary peg into a hillside path, and every morning an old woman moves it three feet so her bench stays outside the works fence.",
  "caption": "Cantonese Guangdong music chamber folk in the 廣東音樂 tradition. Gaohu playing the lead melody with sliding ornaments, yangqin in rippling tremolo, dizi flute in the interludes, soft wood-block percussion, acoustic upright bass holding root notes. Natural room, close wooden resonance, sparse arrangement. Female clear mid-register voice, plain storytelling delivery, melody clearly sung. Clear full voice, every word enunciated, steady sung melody on every line. 80 BPM, D major. Gentle, quietly amused mood. No electric guitar, no drum kit, no synthesizer, no autotune, no rap, no choir.",
  "lyrics": "[Verse]\n星期一朝早 我揹住三腳架\n上山打低 一支紅白樁\n圖紙寫得 清清楚楚\n長櫈嗰邊 要圍起嚟\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n第二朝返嚟 條樁唔見咗\n行開三尺 企咗喺斜坡\n\n[Chorus]\n一支樁 搬嚟搬去\n我量三次 佢移三次\n阿婆坐喺 長櫈度\n話呢個位 睇到日出\n\n[Verse]\n我再打落去 用力啲\n石仔壓住 做記認\n翌日條樁 又行咗路\n樁腳留低 半杯涼茶\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n儀器好準 我知\n但係人心 量唔到\n\n[Chorus]\n一支樁 搬嚟搬去\n我量四次 佢移四次\n阿婆笑住 揮吓把扇\n話後生仔 你慢慢量\n\n[Verse]\n我同組長 打電話\n話呢度 差咗三尺\n佢話你又 量錯數\n我望住張櫈 唔出聲\n\n[Bridge]\n圖紙上面 畫條直線\n山上面 長咗條彎路\n行得多 就變成路\n\n[Chorus]\n一支樁 企喺櫈邊\n我今次 唔再移佢\n阿婆坐喺 長櫈度\n我坐埋去 睇日出\n\n[Outro]\n條線 彎咗少少",
